  "body": "**Hardware:**\r\nRaspberry Pi 4 Model B\r\n**Operating System:**\r\nUbuntu 20.04.2 LTS (GNU/Linux 5.4.0-1032-raspi aarch64)\r\n\r\nAttempted to install the prebuilt Debian/Ubuntu package for the latest stable version of Synapse following the instructions [here](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/INSTALL.md#prebuilt-packages). However, after running `sudo apt update`, `apt` returns the following message:\r\n\r\n`N: Skipping acquire of configured file 'main/binary-arm64/Packages' as repository 'https://packages.matrix.org/debian focal InRelease' doesn't support architecture 'arm64'`",
